From 8da984b03972d6f51b5ab8a9ded71de93eac3190 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] refactor(libc): build the x86-only helpers portably for a
 lifted guest

Under ANYPS5_GUEST_LIFTED the soft-float builtins compute in the
default floating-point environment through <cfenv> and pick NaN results
as x86 does, the 16-byte atomics use __atomic_compare_exchange_n,
Bessel uses std::sqrt and std::fma, and the x86 call-trace thunks and
the setjmp/longjmp assembly are left to the host runtime, which owns
the guest registers. Direct builds are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015taLuK6Ak1pT1P849L2eqq
